-- statement:
--   For the original spectrally negative Lévy process, unchanged filtration, stopped reserve, ruin clock, admissible dividends and exact Stieltjes cash, establish nonnegativity of the stopped reward and its nonnegative ENNReal expected upper bound by the initial candidate value for every cap, including C=top. This is the genuine stochastic HJB/Itô-Dynkin and boundary estimate; it assumes no surrogate law, residual-zero premise or downstream verification theorem. A separately Proved conditional L1/centred-residual bridge can then construct the parent’s integrable witnesses.
